WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:04.520
Hello everyone, welcome back to another episode of the Grand Prixquel Podcast, where we discuss

00:04.520 --> 00:06.000
all things feeder series.

00:06.000 --> 00:11.720
On today's episode, we're going to be doing a review of the E4 finale at Monza, as well

00:11.720 --> 00:16.900
as the British F4 finale at Brands Hatch, I think it's Brands Hatch anyways, as well

00:16.900 --> 00:23.900
as going through the confirmed F2 and F3 seats for 2027 and discussing a few other rumors.

00:23.900 --> 00:27.900
Our hosts for today are myself, Robin, Nova, Peter and Alex.

00:27.900 --> 00:36.900
I guess we should just dive right into the F3 lineups.

00:36.900 --> 00:42.580
So with a post-season testing starting quite soon, I think at the time of recording it's

00:42.580 --> 00:44.620
starting tomorrow actually.

00:44.620 --> 00:49.300
By the time this episode comes out, the first round of testing will be over.

00:49.300 --> 00:52.300
But we have a lot of seat announcements.

00:52.300 --> 00:57.900
I mean, some of them are what we expected, I'd say, but some have been quite surprising.

00:57.900 --> 00:58.900
Not naming teams.

00:58.900 --> 01:06.180
I mean, Trident, we have, of course, KNB and Seb Wheldon, no surprises there, and that's

01:06.180 --> 01:08.140
a very solid lineup.

01:08.140 --> 01:13.500
Third driver is not confirmed, but the less said, the better.

01:13.500 --> 01:16.100
Do we want to talk about Maccagnani?

01:16.100 --> 01:17.500
I mean, what is there to say?

01:17.500 --> 01:21.180
He's basically, he has the money.

01:21.180 --> 01:26.700
If you have the money in this sport, you can pay to go wherever you want.

01:26.700 --> 01:34.140
I mean, we saw, Juan Pablo Montoya said the Invicta seats can go for four million

01:34.140 --> 01:36.540
euros, that's actually insane.

01:36.540 --> 01:37.540
Four million.

01:37.540 --> 01:38.540
Yeah.

01:38.540 --> 01:43.660
I mean, I don't know if we should probably, Trident F3 is like two or three million.

01:43.660 --> 01:49.420
The Campos and Trident F3, because they are the best seats, whereas Campos, if you're

01:49.420 --> 01:52.900
Red Bull Junior, they probably get a bit more pull.

01:52.900 --> 01:55.780
I don't want to talk about Campos.

01:55.780 --> 01:58.020
I don't want to talk about it.

01:58.020 --> 02:02.940
Should we talk about his other team then, he was rumored to?

02:02.940 --> 02:08.980
I still want to mention what we saw this season and what we already talked about, which is

02:08.980 --> 02:18.580
that, while Trident often is really great with the lead car, what we saw with Slater.

02:18.580 --> 02:20.780
They weren't always great with it though.

02:20.780 --> 02:27.620
Second and third car, you know, sometimes it's a thing of talent.

02:27.620 --> 02:33.140
I'm still not over it, but even with like, Freddie, they have technical issues.

02:33.140 --> 02:35.340
I'm not over it, as you can maybe tell.

02:35.340 --> 02:41.540
Let me speak out, because you're interrupting the point I'm making, which is that, you know,

02:41.540 --> 02:48.500
I think it's a problem that I could imagine Trident having, who are not used to, you know,

02:48.500 --> 02:53.220
being in the front, and in Formula 3, you have three cars.

02:53.220 --> 02:57.700
And if we look at the recent lineups, it's pretty clear that they always had someone

02:57.700 --> 03:03.660
like right in front who had, you know, talent, experience, all the things needed, money also

03:03.780 --> 03:09.940
to afford all the stuff, and then you had a pretty clear second and third driver.

03:09.940 --> 03:15.980
And I think it's kind of difficult to rank how far it was a skill issue, which is why

03:15.980 --> 03:25.420
I'm interested to see what KNB and Wheldon will do, because so far I would say, you know,

03:25.420 --> 03:34.980
they should be super close together, but from what I expect from Trident, I think that

03:34.980 --> 03:41.060
they can't put two cars together, and we know that they are pretty focused on one car, because

03:41.060 --> 03:49.020
I remember last year when it was pretty much a thing that they were told again and again,

03:49.020 --> 03:53.940
you know, don't attack Camara, be sure to not do something stupid.

03:53.940 --> 03:58.860
I remember that being told to, I forgot who it was, but I remember it was a whole thing.

03:58.860 --> 04:05.100
That was less of a thing this year, though, I would say, but KNB and Wheldon are-

04:05.100 --> 04:07.780
The issue is just that they weren't close.

04:07.780 --> 04:10.380
I rate them very similarly.

04:10.380 --> 04:13.780
It'll be interesting to see how Trident deals with that.

04:13.780 --> 04:21.860
Honestly, I think I rate Wheldon a bit higher, but I think he has less experience, and I

04:21.860 --> 04:25.460
think that can just be a big problem.

04:25.460 --> 04:35.060
I think moving on to high tech, we have Kanato Le, Michael Shin, and Keanu Al-Azhari confirmed.

04:35.060 --> 04:38.100
I mean, I don't know what to say about this lineup.

04:38.100 --> 04:41.900
A lineup, I guess.

04:41.900 --> 04:46.540
They all exist as drivers.

04:46.540 --> 04:51.260
I mean, I do have something positive to say, Al-Azhari and Al-Dhaheri are both going to be

04:51.260 --> 04:56.100
the first ever Emirati drivers to drive an F3, which I think is really cool.

04:56.100 --> 05:01.180
But yeah, I don't really have much to say about any of these drivers.

05:01.180 --> 05:04.220
I think the next lineup is what I really want to talk about.

05:04.220 --> 05:12.820
Of course, the new team, LN4 Fusion, I mean, the first two names are incredible,

05:12.820 --> 05:13.820
I think.

05:13.820 --> 05:23.420
But we have James Egozi, of course, the reigning EC3 champion, Gabriel Gomez, who was runner

05:23.420 --> 05:28.100
up in Italian F4 last year, and then Dion Gawda.

05:28.100 --> 05:34.220
By the way, Gawda announced as soon as we were preparing to record this episode.

05:34.220 --> 05:35.220
Yeah.

05:35.220 --> 05:40.500
We literally found this out about 15 minutes ago, I think.

05:40.500 --> 05:42.820
We can put the screenshot of the doc on here.

05:42.820 --> 05:45.940
Yeah, I think Evan, get it up.

05:45.940 --> 05:50.100
The live reaction, I'm typing it out and I see Gowda.

05:50.100 --> 05:52.380
And I mean, it's all rookies.

05:52.380 --> 05:57.900
I think Egozi and Gomez, they deserve this, and especially someone like Gomez, who I know

05:57.900 --> 05:59.980
has struggled with funding.

05:59.980 --> 06:03.500
I mean, even Egozi was having funding issues.

06:03.500 --> 06:06.220
It wasn't known whether he'd be doing F3 this year or not.

06:06.220 --> 06:11.140
But I really hope the team is, I guess, semi-decent.

06:11.140 --> 06:16.860
I do want to see some results from these guys, while mainly Egozi and Gomez.

06:16.860 --> 06:20.420
I don't really know what to expect from Gawda.

06:20.420 --> 06:24.020
It's a good lineup for a rookie team, I would feel.

06:24.020 --> 06:26.900
I mean, we couldn't expect three superstars in there.

06:26.900 --> 06:33.220
I mean, there was Alex Powell rumored at some point, but Egozi, Gomez, and Powell.

06:33.220 --> 06:36.980
What a team that would have been, that would have actually been an insane team.

06:37.460 --> 06:40.940
I guess you can't have three broke drivers.

06:40.940 --> 06:44.860
Yeah, you can't have three broke talents, unfortunately.

06:44.860 --> 06:50.620
So good way to link to the next team.

06:50.620 --> 06:55.740
Alex Powell is reportedly joining Prema for next season.

06:55.740 --> 07:00.220
How did he go from Campos to Prema?

07:00.220 --> 07:04.500
He was rumored for, like, throughout the past couple of months.

07:04.500 --> 07:10.940
He was rumored for Campos, F3, alongside Colnaghi and Hanna.

07:10.940 --> 07:16.100
Then he was rumored for Andretti IndyNXT, when he did that one test with them.

07:16.100 --> 07:21.100
And then he was rumored for LN4Fusion, and now he's going to Prema.

07:21.100 --> 07:27.300
And it was announced that he's doing the F3 Post Season Tests with Prema, and he's

07:27.300 --> 07:29.540
also doing the Macau Grand Prix with Prema.

07:29.540 --> 07:33.420
So it's not looking good, guys.

07:33.420 --> 07:38.100
But I think it's fine, because I think we're all being a bit dramatic here.

07:38.100 --> 07:41.580
Obviously, Prema is no Campos and no Trident.

07:41.580 --> 07:51.740
And I think and I expect that LN4Fusion will be, maybe not from the start, but in

07:51.740 --> 07:55.820
at least a few seasons, it will be ahead of Prema and could also be ahead of Prema this

07:55.820 --> 07:56.900
season already.

07:56.900 --> 08:01.460
But overall, if we look back at the last season, they were fine.

08:01.460 --> 08:03.620
They could definitely fight for points.

08:03.620 --> 08:08.740
They had podiums, especially in reverse grid races.

08:08.740 --> 08:12.340
It was oftentimes a good one for them.

08:12.340 --> 08:15.820
And I think you say yourself, Powell is a good driver.

08:15.820 --> 08:20.980
And even if the car is not right, I think he should be able to keep it out of the wall.

08:20.980 --> 08:24.980
He's very good at keeping it out of the wall, unless someone else decides to put him in

08:24.980 --> 08:25.980
the wall.

08:26.540 --> 08:33.340
So personally, I would be really happy if Martin Molnar really got the Prema seat, because

08:33.340 --> 08:34.340
I like him.

08:34.340 --> 08:43.420
And I'm sad to not see Deagen Fairclough anywhere mentioned, because I was hopeful to have some

08:43.420 --> 08:53.420
British help for him by LN4Fusion, but also that he made me realize no Fionn McLaughlin.

08:53.420 --> 08:59.940
I've heard that he might step down to Eurocup-3, but I guess it will depend on what Red Bull

08:59.940 --> 09:01.940
decides to do with him.

09:01.940 --> 09:07.740
Yeah, I just feel bad for him, because I mean, at Silverstone, he did show there was

09:07.740 --> 09:13.340
something there, and British F4 to F3 is a massive step up.

09:13.340 --> 09:18.220
You do got to feel for him, because he had an amazing F4 season last year.

09:18.620 --> 09:24.540
But the thing is also, if you look at him, he didn't step into F4 the second he turned

09:24.540 --> 09:25.540
15.

09:25.540 --> 09:37.420
You know, the money is always an issue, and I think what he and Red Bull probably tried

09:37.420 --> 09:44.820
to do was repeat what Tsolov did, which was after he won Spanish F4, he did three seasons

09:44.820 --> 09:53.060
in F3, because from what I remember he said, while it's more expensive, it also pays out

09:53.060 --> 09:56.620
a lot more from sponsors and people interested.

09:56.620 --> 10:02.300
If you do that instead of going season to FREC or back down to FREC  or anything

10:02.300 --> 10:09.900
similar, because as much as I respect your capacity, so no sponsor really, like there

10:09.900 --> 10:14.260
are some sponsors obviously who care about it, but if you're in F3, you just have a

10:15.140 --> 10:23.540
more international reach, you can say, look, I'm at the F1 weekend, I'm racing at the same

10:23.540 --> 10:32.820
time as them, you know, in most countries the F3 stream is on the same channel as the

10:32.820 --> 10:40.980
F1 stream, so there's just a huge step up, but if he couldn't afford it, and if Red Bull

10:40.980 --> 10:45.940
says, hey, we do have other drivers, so we care about more, because you know, it's Red

10:45.940 --> 10:52.100
Bull, while if I remember correctly, Tsolov was with Alpine at the time, that's just how

10:52.100 --> 10:53.700
it is, I fear.

10:53.700 --> 11:00.020
But yeah, back to the Prema lineup, alongside, for testing at least, alongside Powell and

11:00.020 --> 11:07.220
Molnar, there's also Nakamura, honestly, I don't know, I feel like he was pretty okay

11:08.020 --> 11:17.460
this season in F3, way better than his teammates, at least, but also I've heard that this lineup,

11:17.460 --> 11:24.660
the testing lineup, isn't going to be the same lineup for 2027, and that instead of Molnar,

11:24.660 --> 11:26.180
it'll probably be Perard.

11:26.180 --> 11:38.580
Having really bad flashbacks to Portimao in Eurocup-3, and the concept of having Perard

11:38.580 --> 11:46.900
be Powell's teammate is scary, because I mean, like I mentioned, Powell doesn't put it in

11:46.900 --> 11:53.140
the wall by himself, but if there's someone else putting him in the wall for him, I don't

11:53.140 --> 11:55.540
know, guys, I give up.

11:55.620 --> 12:00.500
Oh, what I just remembered was, I think it's really interesting how many different rumours

12:00.500 --> 12:07.060
there are, but also how many of them just seem to turn completely wrong, so I'm kind

12:07.060 --> 12:11.860
of on the edge of saying, you know, it could all happen, but I would not be surprised at

12:11.860 --> 12:16.420
all if we see some more real big surprises.

12:16.420 --> 12:22.820
I mean, LN4Fusion, I think did great, because none of the rumoured drivers really went anywhere,

12:23.460 --> 12:30.980
Yeah, weren't we saying, like, Yevan David and Fernando Barrichello, and then I don't

12:30.980 --> 12:35.780
remember who the last one was, but we were not saying it was Egozi, Gomez or Gowda.

12:36.580 --> 12:43.860
Yeah, I mean, we were so surprised with especially Gomez and Gowda, like, it came out of nowhere.

12:43.860 --> 12:49.860
I think they're keeping it under wraps really well, and while I do like some rumours and

12:49.860 --> 12:54.260
some discussions, I think it's probably a good thing for everyone involved.

12:54.260 --> 13:00.180
And it's also fun sometimes when you wake up and you see a driver that you like surprisingly

13:00.180 --> 13:01.540
getting signed to a good team.

13:02.500 --> 13:03.620
Hell yeah, let's do it.

13:04.420 --> 13:05.540
I can't imagine.

13:06.500 --> 13:15.540
Anyways, so moving on to the MP lineup, which De Palo got announced earlier today to be

13:15.540 --> 13:23.140
racing for MP, we still don't know who the other two seats are, but it's looking very,

13:23.140 --> 13:29.940
very unlikely for both Ean Eyckmans and René Lammers to be getting F3 seats, at least with MP,

13:29.940 --> 13:34.100
because from what we've heard, it's supposed to be Newman Chi and Maciej Gladysz.

13:36.100 --> 13:43.380
I feel like MP really, really disappointed me last season, because we are the last few scenes,

13:43.380 --> 13:49.780
because we had some really, not great always, but we had some good drivers,

13:49.780 --> 13:54.500
and we had some really nice lineups, and we did have some drivers that I think are great,

13:54.500 --> 13:56.580
but they just keep shitting in the back.

13:58.100 --> 14:06.580
It's so disappointing, because you expect more from MP than, you know, some P15 finishes.

14:07.540 --> 14:16.900
I think Van Amersfoort, we have, I'm not even going to try it, Al Dhaheri and Yevan David and...

14:17.860 --> 14:18.820
It's Deligny.

14:20.340 --> 14:21.700
He says Deligny.

14:22.260 --> 14:23.860
It's meant to be De-lih-ny, really.

14:24.923 --> 14:27.074
Mispronouncing his own name is crazy.

14:27.220 --> 14:28.980
I don't, I refuse to learn.

14:31.380 --> 14:34.020
I love the French, but I make an exception for this one.

14:34.020 --> 14:43.380
The point is, I think this is a really, it's a nice lineup, I think, it's not a great lineup,

14:43.380 --> 14:52.020
it's not an ‘oh wow!’ lineup, but it's three drivers that I think, all of them, pretty much they deserve

14:52.020 --> 15:00.260
a chance in F3, you know, I did expect a bit more from Deliny, Deligny, who knows, but Van Amersfoort

15:00.260 --> 15:07.220
also just, you know, they were good, but obviously, they can't keep up with Trident and Campers.

15:07.780 --> 15:09.140
It's fine, it's fine.

15:10.020 --> 15:16.500
I think for most of us, Yevan David was really stand out, kind of unexpected driver last season,

15:16.500 --> 15:25.140
because he was clearly the best at AIX, and I think while he did stand out, I'm excited to see

15:26.100 --> 15:33.220
I'm excited to see what he will do when, you know, his teammates are also drivers that are not

15:33.220 --> 15:34.820
expected to **** the bag, basically.

15:36.180 --> 15:38.420
Yeah, I think it's a pretty solid lineup.

15:39.460 --> 15:45.460
I think for Yevan David, it's really make or break, because if he's also here pretty good,

15:45.460 --> 15:52.500
he can definitely do the step up to, you know, F2, and F1 is not in reach for like anyone, but

15:53.140 --> 15:59.860
I think he can do something good, but if he, in comparison to Al-Dhaheri and the other driver,

15:59.860 --> 16:02.020
does not perform and shows he's, you know,

16:06.020 --> 16:12.900
the level that you'd expect from, you know, an average good driver, it's not a driver that you

16:12.900 --> 16:16.340
think, wow, it's a generational talent, they're going to make it to F1.

16:16.340 --> 16:21.540
It's not like Freddie Slater or Camara where it's like, obviously, they don't make it.

16:21.540 --> 16:27.380
I think it's also not like some drivers where you might think, hey, if they're in the right

16:27.380 --> 16:33.140
position at the right time, like Ugochukwu, they can also make it to F1.

16:33.140 --> 16:39.060
It's drivers that I think they're good, if they're really lucky, a chance could come their way,

16:39.700 --> 16:48.260
but I think doing good in F3, F2, it still helps to get a good seat elsewhere.

16:48.260 --> 16:55.940
If you fail in F3, you could be sent back to, you know, Eurocup 3 or GB3 or something.

16:55.940 --> 16:57.540
Or Euro Formula Open.

16:58.420 --> 17:05.860
Euro Formula Open is actually a sad one, but if you graduate from F2, it does not always have to

17:05.860 --> 17:14.340
be, and I just remember we got a new Formula E team, which sounds like fake LN4 Fusion, but it's

17:14.340 --> 17:19.300
fine. The whole point is they can go somewhere.

17:19.300 --> 17:20.660
And I'm excited to see that.

17:20.660 --> 17:27.860
I'm excited to see more drivers go into the general world of motorsports, because otherwise

17:27.860 --> 17:33.300
you end up like Alessandro Giusti, who's doing third season with Rodin in F3.

17:35.300 --> 17:37.780
I don't know how to feel about the Rodin lineup.

17:37.780 --> 17:39.780
I need to be reminded.

17:39.780 --> 17:44.980
I remember Giusti was in MP in 2025.

17:45.940 --> 17:47.460
Was he also in 2026?

17:48.020 --> 17:48.340
Yes.

17:48.980 --> 17:56.820
Okay, I think Rodin is a step up because, you know, they did fairly well this season, I would say.

17:56.820 --> 17:58.820
Or am I misremembering things?

17:58.820 --> 18:06.180
Because I remember Brando Badoer was with them and he was, wasn't he top five for majority of

18:06.180 --> 18:07.300
the championship?

18:07.300 --> 18:07.860
He was.

18:07.860 --> 18:08.660
Yeah.

18:08.660 --> 18:10.580
Pretty high up for like most of the season.

18:10.580 --> 18:18.740
I think Alessandro Giusti should be able to be on par with Brando Badoer.

18:18.740 --> 18:20.660
That's my, that's my call.

18:20.660 --> 18:27.860
I will say, though, regarding the other drivers for Rodin, I'm disappointed there's no Alex

18:27.860 --> 18:28.900
Ninovic.

18:28.900 --> 18:31.220
How do we have Seewooruthun and not Ninovic?

18:32.100 --> 18:32.500
Exactly.

18:32.500 --> 18:33.300
It's because of money.

18:34.100 --> 18:35.860
Yeah, I think, I think that's sad.

18:35.860 --> 18:41.140
I really like Pedro Clerot and I think, from what I remember from last season, I think

18:41.940 --> 18:42.820
he was good.

18:42.820 --> 18:43.380
I like him.

18:43.940 --> 18:47.300
It could be that he could bring a real fight with Giusti.

18:47.300 --> 18:54.020
I'm really, I'm sad that Ninovic isn't really in discussions anywhere because the concept of

18:54.020 --> 19:01.300
winning GB3 and then going to FREC and then doing another year of FREC, that's really sad.

19:02.020 --> 19:06.820
And I think he should be in, he should be on the F3 grid more than, sort of.

19:07.460 --> 19:11.220
I am biased for other reasons, but I do not like Seewooruthun.

19:11.860 --> 19:14.660
And yeah, I have my reasons.

19:14.660 --> 19:18.020
Onto teams that don't have any drivers announced.

19:19.220 --> 19:20.500
Wait, did we mention Campos?

19:21.140 --> 19:23.060
I vaguely mentioned it.

19:23.060 --> 19:24.260
Okay, let's go to Campos.

19:24.820 --> 19:28.580
I vaguely mentioned this, but Campos is going to be,

19:29.380 --> 19:32.740
reportedly going to be Rivera, Hanna, and Colnaghi.

19:32.740 --> 19:38.180
Rivera and Hanna have been announced, Colnaghi has not, but I think it's very obvious anyways.

19:39.780 --> 19:41.620
I don't want to talk more about the Campos lineup.

19:41.620 --> 19:44.340
If you guys want to talk about it, that's fine, but I'm going to shut up.

19:45.060 --> 19:47.140
I think it's fine.

19:47.140 --> 19:51.380
No, it's, I mean, it's, it's alright lineup, like all around.

19:51.380 --> 19:55.380
It's fine drivers who could do something, but from last season, it's too mean.

19:55.380 --> 20:01.540
Colnaghi is pretty good, but I, and Rivera should really be a title challenger.

20:02.820 --> 20:03.940
I'm not saying they're bad.

20:04.740 --> 20:12.660
I'm just saying that in the whole direction of Theophile Nael, Ugo Ugochukwu, I think those two,

20:12.660 --> 20:18.100
and before that, Tsolov at least, I don't know what Boya did that one season,

20:18.100 --> 20:22.980
where he suddenly halfway through became the fastest driver ever.

20:22.980 --> 20:24.340
But all right.

20:24.340 --> 20:28.820
The point is, it was the third driver. It was the Aston Martin academy thing.

20:28.820 --> 20:29.320
Wasn't it?

20:29.780 --> 20:30.980
Tasanapol?

20:30.980 --> 20:35.620
It could be, but I also think he did pretty well at the end of the season then.

20:35.620 --> 20:36.100
I don't know.

20:36.100 --> 20:38.900
Maybe Campos just took the step up there, but the point is,

20:39.460 --> 20:44.500
it was lineups that could definitely fight for the title and that won the title.

20:45.700 --> 20:49.300
Now the thing is, I don't think they're bad drivers.

20:49.300 --> 20:54.660
I think they're good drivers, but there's a difference between good

20:55.220 --> 20:57.940
and right up there fighting for championships.

20:59.940 --> 21:06.020
I feel like that's just not something that I expect from any of those drivers.

21:06.020 --> 21:08.340
Maybe it can be their standout season to me.

21:08.340 --> 21:09.380
That could be.

21:09.380 --> 21:15.140
I would not be opposed to having a driver do a standout season.

21:16.020 --> 21:17.940
A bit aided by car performance.

21:19.700 --> 21:22.180
Maybe a bit aided by Trident issues.

21:22.180 --> 21:26.500
But so far, I'm not on the way.

21:26.500 --> 21:30.740
That last year where I was like, pretty much it's clear that we're going to see

21:32.180 --> 21:35.380
a fight between Campos and Trident.

21:36.260 --> 21:38.100
I think I'm going to have to disagree here.

21:38.100 --> 21:43.620
While I'm not moved by Hanna at all, I think seeing Rivera's performance

21:43.620 --> 21:46.980
after missing the season opener this season,

21:46.980 --> 21:49.300
I think he really should be fighting for the title.

21:49.300 --> 21:51.460
And Colnaghi's a really good driver as well.

21:51.460 --> 21:56.020
So I think they should probably be able to take the fight to KNB and Wheldon.

21:58.100 --> 21:59.380
But yeah, maybe that's just me.

22:00.260 --> 22:02.820
I think it's more aided.

22:02.820 --> 22:03.860
I think it will happen.

22:03.860 --> 22:08.660
But again, to me, probably more aided by the car.

22:11.940 --> 22:13.060
But we'll see.

22:13.060 --> 22:16.020
We'll leave possibilities open.

22:16.020 --> 22:16.740
We're going to see.

22:18.260 --> 22:19.860
Do we speak about all teams now?

22:20.900 --> 22:25.700
Yeah, I want to move on to the teams that haven't really had any driver announcements,

22:25.700 --> 22:28.500
though we have seen some rumors for some of them.

22:29.300 --> 22:33.060
ART, I'm really excited for ART.

22:33.060 --> 22:36.020
Just because Olivieri has been testing for them.

22:36.740 --> 22:42.900
And I'm really happy that Olivieri is getting an F3 seat.

22:42.980 --> 22:45.860
Because I was really worried that even after winning the FREC title,

22:45.860 --> 22:47.220
he wouldn't be able to get a seat.

22:47.940 --> 22:53.620
But he is, probably, unless ART decide to change their minds for whatever reason.

22:53.620 --> 22:55.540
But like I said, he has been testing for them.

22:55.540 --> 22:59.700
So I'm really excited to see what he can do next year.

23:01.460 --> 23:06.900
But alongside Olivieri, I'm a bit less sure about these ones

23:06.900 --> 23:10.020
because we haven't really seen any testing or anything.

23:13.060 --> 23:18.580
We're supposed to have Enzo Yeh, who has been rumored for a while.

23:18.580 --> 23:22.740
And then I don't know about the last seat I've heard that might be Taito Kato.

23:23.620 --> 23:25.620
But I don't know.

23:27.380 --> 23:32.900
I think the ART seats are the ones that have been the most flip-floppity,

23:32.900 --> 23:35.460
I don't know, in terms of the drivers who might take them.

23:36.100 --> 23:40.260
I hear Olivieri a lot, but the other two have always been a bit

23:40.900 --> 23:44.820
up in the air, is what I wanted to say, not flip-floppity.

23:44.820 --> 23:47.300
Up in the air as to who will actually take them.

23:48.020 --> 23:49.540
I like the word flip-floppity.

23:53.220 --> 23:54.980
And then we have DAMS.

23:56.660 --> 23:57.540
What is going on there?

23:58.180 --> 24:00.340
Have we heard anything?

24:00.980 --> 24:03.460
Pretty much dead last, so it doesn't really matter anyways.

24:04.340 --> 24:07.700
Yeah, I've only heard Abhkazava.

24:08.660 --> 24:10.820
And even that's not super clear.

24:14.340 --> 24:16.260
I don't know who else they could have.

24:17.300 --> 24:21.940
We're missing someone that's coming from, like, really out of the blue.

24:23.540 --> 24:26.660
From some championship where you'll be like, why are you coming here?

24:26.660 --> 24:27.540
We were missing that.

24:29.140 --> 24:32.020
And I mean, archivably, there's a bunch of those drivers.

24:32.660 --> 24:34.180
Who won Euroformula Open?

24:34.820 --> 24:35.380
Enzo Yeh.

24:36.020 --> 24:36.740
Yeh.

24:36.740 --> 24:38.100
But he's the only one.

24:38.100 --> 24:40.340
Who else competed in Euroformula Open?

24:41.220 --> 24:46.980
Everett Stack left the championship halfway through.

24:46.980 --> 24:51.460
Carrasquedo was there, but I think he's rumored for an F2 seat.

24:51.460 --> 24:51.780
What?

24:52.420 --> 24:55.380
Yeah, he's apparently rumored for VAR F2.

24:55.380 --> 25:02.260
Okay, so all the fun that we are missing out in F3, we're getting in F2 this season.

25:03.060 --> 25:07.780
We need to talk about F2 in a minute because I just remembered something hilarious.

25:07.780 --> 25:08.980
Should we just go on?

25:08.980 --> 25:11.380
Because DAMS is irrelevant anyways.

25:12.020 --> 25:14.020
Yeah, DAMS sounds like no one tied to a seat.

25:14.020 --> 25:16.100
F2 now.

25:16.100 --> 25:19.220
If we're getting into F2, I have a question.

25:20.260 --> 25:27.060
Whom of you remembers that first F2 reserve driver guy where they said

25:27.140 --> 25:30.100
they would prepare for the whole season 2020?

25:30.100 --> 25:31.540
Will he appear?

25:32.820 --> 25:35.620
I've heard that they took down his page on their website.

25:36.580 --> 25:38.180
He was connected to VAR, right?

25:38.900 --> 25:40.420
Yeah, he was their reserve driver.

25:41.060 --> 25:41.940
It was something orange.

25:41.940 --> 25:45.140
It was either VAR or MP.

25:45.140 --> 25:53.380
If I remember correctly, wasn't he placed below Nicole Havrda in the whole season at some point?

25:54.660 --> 25:56.820
That is really fascinating.

25:56.900 --> 25:57.620
That's not good.

25:57.620 --> 25:58.580
I'm your field driver.

25:58.580 --> 26:00.340
We were missing that fun here.

26:02.580 --> 26:10.820
Although I'm going to be honest, so far the F2 grid is not inspiring anything for me really.

26:12.100 --> 26:13.460
Yeah, I don't know.

26:16.180 --> 26:18.020
I'm scared about MP. LVH?

26:18.660 --> 26:29.620
I'm not scared of Laurens Van Hoepen,I’m scared of the possibility of Alex Dunne doing a third F2 season.

26:29.620 --> 26:30.900
Oh, I forgot about that.

26:31.700 --> 26:32.340
Who?

26:32.340 --> 26:33.060
Alex Dunne.

26:33.940 --> 26:34.340
Dunne.

26:36.740 --> 26:40.180
He crashed into Victor Martins one too many times.

26:40.180 --> 26:41.860
He just inherited his luck.

26:41.860 --> 26:43.140
It's crazy how that works.

26:43.780 --> 26:47.860
So rumor says that if Alex Dunne does not win the championship this year,

26:48.180 --> 26:52.580
he will be returning for a third F2 season with MP Motorsport.

26:53.540 --> 26:55.300
With MP Motorsport?

26:56.100 --> 26:57.780
Oh my god, that's a step down.

26:59.140 --> 27:01.860
MP is worse than Rodin.

27:01.860 --> 27:02.740
What is he doing?

27:03.460 --> 27:06.580
MP has the ability to be really...

27:06.580 --> 27:08.740
We're seeing it this season with Gabriele Mini,

27:08.740 --> 27:14.100
who I think could be far ahead, far further in the championship.

27:14.180 --> 27:15.700
But MP just sometimes...

27:17.060 --> 27:18.020
It just doesn't work.

27:18.900 --> 27:19.700
It's just...

27:19.700 --> 27:21.540
No, we're not performing this week.

27:21.540 --> 27:23.460
No, we don't feel like performing.

27:23.460 --> 27:23.940
Why not?

27:24.500 --> 27:25.940
This is crazy.

27:25.940 --> 27:30.500
But MP does have Laurens van Hoepen announced.

27:30.500 --> 27:31.140
Van Hopen?

27:31.140 --> 27:32.020
Van Hoepen?

27:32.020 --> 27:32.580
Van Hoepen.

27:33.940 --> 27:34.260
Yeah.

27:34.260 --> 27:35.620
It's a Dutch name, I refuse.

27:36.180 --> 27:40.500
I don't know what their plan is if Dunne does win the championship.

27:41.220 --> 27:42.820
Who do they bring in then?

27:42.820 --> 27:44.100
I think it'll just be...

27:44.900 --> 27:45.460
Do all...

27:49.940 --> 27:50.580
What's the word?

27:51.300 --> 27:56.020
Do all high-rated F3 drivers from last season have a seat?

27:56.660 --> 27:59.220
I mean, as far as I've heard...

28:00.740 --> 28:03.140
Are we talking this season or last year?

28:03.140 --> 28:06.500
Like this season, who's still open on the market?

28:06.500 --> 28:07.380
Who could still...

28:07.380 --> 28:12.180
I've heard that Bruno Del Pino is going to IndyNXT.

28:12.180 --> 28:15.140
But I've also heard that he might end up in F2.

28:15.140 --> 28:16.420
He's broke as f***.

28:17.300 --> 28:22.740
Which is crazy considering his uncle works in an F1 team.

28:22.740 --> 28:23.780
Get some money, bro.

28:24.340 --> 28:25.540
Use the nepotism.

28:26.100 --> 28:27.140
Just don't be broke.

28:27.940 --> 28:28.340
Come on.

28:29.220 --> 28:32.580
I think at the moment his uncle is with Aston Martin.

28:33.620 --> 28:34.340
What's his name?

28:34.340 --> 28:35.060
I forgot his name.

28:35.060 --> 28:36.260
I know his face.

28:37.300 --> 28:38.580
Pedro de la Rosa?

28:39.540 --> 28:42.820
He's either with Ferrari or Aston Martin doing some work with him.

28:43.860 --> 28:44.500
Get that boy seat.

28:44.500 --> 28:45.380
He's with Aston Martin.

28:46.020 --> 28:47.060
Aston Martin is.

28:47.620 --> 28:48.180
Bullsh**.

28:48.180 --> 28:51.780
Just adopt that guy into the junior team.

28:51.780 --> 28:54.100
You can get any guy, really.

28:55.620 --> 28:57.460
What about Boya?

28:58.980 --> 29:02.420
I heard Leon somewhere, but I don't remember where he was supposed to go.

29:02.420 --> 29:03.780
I don't know.

29:03.780 --> 29:05.060
There was too much going on in this F2.

29:05.300 --> 29:11.620
He's the kind of driver that I could see returning and doing a season with MP, if he can afford it.

29:13.220 --> 29:14.580
I feel it in my heart.

29:14.580 --> 29:15.540
That's what he could do.

29:16.100 --> 29:16.980
Yeah, I can see it.

29:18.580 --> 29:22.980
I think it's more likely than Dunne doing a third season because I thought he was

29:22.980 --> 29:29.300
poor and recently got like 30,000 euros, which sounds a lot to a normal person,

29:29.300 --> 29:31.140
but in F2 it's like...

29:31.940 --> 29:33.380
Formation lap, basically.

29:33.940 --> 29:34.660
It's like a tip.

29:35.460 --> 29:36.660
Formation lap.

29:36.660 --> 29:39.220
But yeah, I don't know what's going on at MP.

29:39.780 --> 29:42.820
I don't really think I want to know what's going on at MP.

29:43.700 --> 29:46.500
It's sad because I would like to like MP.

29:47.300 --> 29:48.500
Anyways, Rodin.

29:49.460 --> 29:52.260
I think Brando Badoer stepping up after, I'm going to be honest,

29:52.900 --> 29:56.420
his F3 season surprised me positively.

29:56.420 --> 30:03.140
So I think it's honestly one of the few seats where I'm weirdly okay with it

30:03.140 --> 30:07.060
or would be happy about it because I think he had a good F3 season.

30:07.060 --> 30:09.540
He's stepping up with the same team to F2.

30:09.540 --> 30:10.340
Why not, you know?

30:10.340 --> 30:11.220
I don't expect a lot of it.

30:11.220 --> 30:16.420
I feel like this has been expected for a while, like him stepping up to F2 with Rodin.

30:16.420 --> 30:20.420
But I think it's what I expect from Formula 2.

30:20.420 --> 30:22.100
It's what I want to see.

30:22.980 --> 30:27.220
It's also in the list of, you know, afterwards, maybe seen somewhere else,

30:27.220 --> 30:30.500
but it's a good overall thing.

30:31.460 --> 30:33.460
But who's going to be in the second Rodin seat?

30:34.020 --> 30:35.060
You know what?

30:35.060 --> 30:36.100
Fuck F3.

30:36.100 --> 30:36.980
We don't need it.

30:36.980 --> 30:40.980
We're going to send Alex Ninovic straight to F2.

30:40.980 --> 30:44.500
If Antonelli can do it, he can do it too.

30:44.500 --> 30:46.340
That's my reasoning.

30:46.980 --> 30:47.940
No, he's too poor.

30:47.940 --> 30:48.740
He can't afford that.

30:49.540 --> 30:50.660
If there's a will, there's a way.

30:51.460 --> 30:56.980
I think we have very few rumors for F2 seats

30:57.620 --> 31:00.100
because, you know, the championship isn't tied up yet.

31:00.180 --> 31:09.860
So quite a few people are still like, if he doesn't win, Dunne can return.

31:10.740 --> 31:12.820
Gabriele Mini can return if he doesn't like.

31:12.820 --> 31:17.220
That's three drivers that are kind of, they can't sign anything yet

31:17.220 --> 31:19.780
because, you know, who knows?

31:20.500 --> 31:23.300
Who knows what's going to, I mean, Gabriele Mini is more like,

31:24.260 --> 31:26.900
but, you know, you can't be too sure about it.

31:26.900 --> 31:30.980
It'll also depend if he finishes fourth or if he can make his way up

31:30.980 --> 31:33.380
and finish maybe second or third.

31:33.380 --> 31:34.980
You know, that will make a huge difference.

31:36.420 --> 31:41.700
So I feel like F2 is very open, but we have the disadvantage that F3

31:41.700 --> 31:45.060
is pretty much set, it has to be set earlier.

31:45.620 --> 31:53.460
So good F3 drivers from last season can't be sure if they should return to F3

31:53.460 --> 31:56.420
because F2s be bullshitting.

31:56.420 --> 31:59.380
Who do we, who else do we want to see with Rodin?

31:59.380 --> 32:04.740
Well, I don't have a name right now, but recently.

32:04.740 --> 32:07.860
Explain his face.

32:08.580 --> 32:10.660
I thought we were playing guess who?

32:11.460 --> 32:15.300
I mean, I think Stenshorne is important to mention,

32:15.300 --> 32:19.460
but I heard somewhere that he is definitely not returning.

32:19.460 --> 32:22.900
But you're right, I remember there was a rumor for the Rodin seat,

32:22.900 --> 32:24.420
which is why he's not returning.

32:24.420 --> 32:27.780
But I don't remember at all who, I don't even remember her face.

32:28.500 --> 32:30.180
I just remember hearing it.

32:30.180 --> 32:34.020
Yeah, and he's also gone and done the IndyNXT test.

32:34.020 --> 32:38.180
But I mean, a lot of people have been doing IndyNXT, like Alex Palou.

32:38.180 --> 32:44.260
I don't think everyone who does the IndyNXT test.

32:44.260 --> 32:47.300
I think the reason Palou did it was because the driver

32:47.300 --> 32:50.820
that was originally meant to be there was either sick or injured.

32:50.820 --> 32:51.860
I don't remember which one.

32:52.740 --> 32:55.780
I think I thought he just wanted to do it because it's cool.

32:56.500 --> 33:02.260
Anyways, I found it and it says Noel Leon should probably join Rodan,

33:02.260 --> 33:04.260
which I think it's fine.

33:04.260 --> 33:05.620
I think he has a good season.

33:05.620 --> 33:06.580
I think it's fine.

33:07.460 --> 33:11.220
But I think it's also his rookie season.

33:11.220 --> 33:15.300
So while Campos is better, we go to get to Campos in a second.

33:15.300 --> 33:16.660
I think it's fine.

33:17.460 --> 33:20.580
I mean, I think the issue isn't that he's outbidding Stenshorne.

33:20.580 --> 33:23.860
I think the issue is Stenshorne has like three bucks to his name

33:23.860 --> 33:28.260
because no one really in Norway really cares.

33:28.260 --> 33:30.500
But which is sad because from what I remember,

33:30.500 --> 33:35.060
that's a lot of his career, even though he's had some great moments.

33:35.060 --> 33:35.540
Where was it?

33:35.540 --> 33:40.420
It was some Formula 4 or FREC series where he finished second to Antonelli.

33:40.420 --> 33:41.940
It was really good from him.

33:41.940 --> 33:43.700
That might have been FRECA.

33:43.700 --> 33:45.860
Yeah, I don't remember which one it was.

33:45.860 --> 33:47.620
I just remember it happened.

33:47.700 --> 33:52.420
Invicta is the only team that is really officially set.

33:52.420 --> 33:56.900
You know what team he finished second again?

33:56.900 --> 33:57.860
It was R-ace GP.

33:58.660 --> 34:00.340
I had to get my R-ace GP mention. Of course, of course.

34:04.500 --> 34:05.860
But are you happy about it?

34:06.580 --> 34:12.500
Are you glad that your team was able to help him have a nice career so far?

34:13.780 --> 34:14.980
Are you proud of your team?

34:14.980 --> 34:17.300
I'm proud of my stupid French team.

34:18.420 --> 34:22.900
You can't say they're stupid a second after we said they did really well.

34:22.900 --> 34:23.540
Okay, fine.

34:23.540 --> 34:26.660
I'm proud of my not stupid French team.

34:26.660 --> 34:31.380
Of the competent competitive team once in a while.

34:32.100 --> 34:33.460
Either ways, Invicta.

34:33.460 --> 34:34.660
Invicta, who's ready?

34:35.300 --> 34:37.860
Sadly, Peter isn't here anymore.

34:38.740 --> 34:42.020
Is it a surprise that Freddie Slater is going to Invicta?

34:42.020 --> 34:43.780
I think I'm going to be honest right now.

34:43.780 --> 34:44.020
No.

34:44.660 --> 34:47.620
I think that's one of the things that makes F2 boring to me

34:47.620 --> 34:50.980
because we all know he's going to have an F1 seat in 2028 anyways.

34:50.980 --> 34:52.820
He could totally **** the bag.

34:52.820 --> 34:54.820
He could come dead last in every race.

34:54.820 --> 34:59.220
He could get a race, but he would still end up in F1 in 2028.

34:59.220 --> 35:01.220
That contract is signed.

35:01.220 --> 35:04.660
The Invicta contract was signed February this year or something.

35:04.660 --> 35:08.100
I remember before F3 testing started,

35:08.900 --> 35:14.580
I saw someone point out that he already had a signed contract with Invicta for F2.

35:15.460 --> 35:17.140
I have an issue with him personally,

35:18.660 --> 35:26.020
but I have a bigger liking for drivers who don't have as much money.

35:26.820 --> 35:28.260
I mean, he kind of deserves it.

35:28.260 --> 35:32.500
He does well, but I can't be in favor of that.

35:33.460 --> 35:37.060
Is everyone just dying all the time or is it my Wi-Fi?

35:37.140 --> 35:39.380
I think it's a bit of both, honestly.

35:39.380 --> 35:42.740
Because whenever I finish a sentence, just no one speaks it out.

35:42.740 --> 35:43.220
Oh my God.

35:43.860 --> 35:44.900
Do they hate me?

35:48.260 --> 35:51.620
I think I was more surprised about the second Invicta seed.

35:52.580 --> 35:52.900
Yes.

35:53.460 --> 35:54.900
Where did Stromsted come from?

35:55.460 --> 36:00.580
Yeah, I think the strongest rumor was Leon for a while.

36:00.580 --> 36:02.100
I think that was Mass Delusion.

36:03.380 --> 36:05.220
Oh, well, I saw a lot of Leon.

36:05.220 --> 36:08.420
But I think Noel Leon would have made sense.

36:09.140 --> 36:12.180
Yeah, I'm surprised from Stromsted.

36:12.180 --> 36:19.220
Honestly, my assumption, my expectation was kind of that Boya would get the seed.

36:21.140 --> 36:26.980
Because Invicta has, for the last three seasons, had the exact same lineup,

36:26.980 --> 36:33.940
which was always the number one driver who brings in a bit of sponsors,

36:33.940 --> 36:35.060
a bit of help and all of that.

36:35.060 --> 36:40.820
Who's like the brick priority coming straight from winning F3 with Trident.

36:40.820 --> 36:46.580
And the second driver is usually a driver that has at least a year of experience,

36:46.580 --> 36:51.220
since he's probably more someone who everyone's kind of aware

36:51.220 --> 36:53.460
that they cannot fight the first driver.

36:53.460 --> 36:57.860
That was, from what I remember, Kush Maini, Roman Stanek.

36:57.860 --> 37:00.660
And now it's Joshua Durksen.

37:01.540 --> 37:05.220
You know, there's clear picture there.

37:05.220 --> 37:08.100
And Stromsted doesn't really fit into that.

37:08.740 --> 37:12.180
My gut was saying Ollie Goethe for the same reasons.

37:13.300 --> 37:13.780
You know what?

37:13.780 --> 37:16.340
Ollie Goethe would have also been one that I would have believed.

37:17.300 --> 37:21.460
But I felt like it just does not feel like an Ollie Goethe place.

37:21.460 --> 37:22.900
He could also return with MP.

37:22.900 --> 37:24.500
Maybe he's the one returning with MP.

37:25.300 --> 37:25.800
Maybe.

37:27.940 --> 37:28.580
Moving on.

37:29.540 --> 37:37.060
We need to discuss a big elephant in the room, which is Durksen Hitech.

37:37.940 --> 37:39.940
He's a big Paraguayan elephant.

37:39.940 --> 37:44.180
You did a season with Invicta and you came.

37:45.940 --> 37:48.500
If you did a season with Invicta, you're not allowed to return.

37:48.500 --> 37:53.860
Because honestly, it's like his fifth season or so.

37:53.860 --> 38:01.540
Is he not equaling the win record or something?

38:01.540 --> 38:03.780
Yeah, he has equaled the win record, I think.

38:04.580 --> 38:06.580
That is bullsh**.

38:07.380 --> 38:08.580
Why would he return?

38:09.300 --> 38:10.660
What is he looking for?

38:10.660 --> 38:13.940
And I see people online going, oh, he should get an F1 seat.

38:15.060 --> 38:16.740
What should he get an F1 seat for?

38:16.740 --> 38:21.460
I don't think he even qualifies for an FP1 license.

38:22.420 --> 38:23.780
But I'm not quite sure about that.

38:23.780 --> 38:25.460
Honestly, someone fact-checked me.

38:25.460 --> 38:30.340
But I've had some insane people in my comments being like,

38:30.340 --> 38:35.300
oh, everyone in Paraguay is very glad because he will make it to F1.

38:36.500 --> 38:37.540
Who told you that?

38:37.540 --> 38:39.220
Who the hell is making it to F1?

38:39.220 --> 38:40.660
Because it's not Durksen.

38:42.660 --> 38:43.540
Mass delusion.

38:43.540 --> 38:44.660
That's mass delusion.

38:45.700 --> 38:47.220
It's actually crazy.

38:47.220 --> 38:48.740
What are we talking about?

38:48.740 --> 38:49.540
I'm sorry.

38:49.620 --> 38:56.100
