56:23.720 --> 56:27.000
I think he's been rumored to be doing another F3 season.

56:27.000 --> 56:29.160
I mentioned this when we were talking about ART.

56:30.040 --> 56:36.280
Yeah, but he's the last one that I wouldn't be opposed to seeing him in F2 with LN4 Fusion.

56:36.360 --> 56:42.280
But again, I think we won't see anything rumored happening,

56:42.280 --> 56:46.440
because I think they're keeping it under wraps, and I think that's good.

56:46.440 --> 56:50.600
Yeah, and either way, we can't really have the announcements anytime soon,

56:50.600 --> 56:54.200
because they're not officially confirmed to be in F2 yet.

56:57.000 --> 56:58.360
Is that it for rumors?

56:58.360 --> 57:00.760
I can't really think of anything else.

57:01.640 --> 57:04.680
Yeah, that's all I've heard.

57:05.480 --> 57:09.480
We might be forgetting something, but I don't know.

57:09.480 --> 57:14.440
If we forgot something, because we don't like a driver, who cares?

57:15.400 --> 57:22.280
So if we're done with rumors, I do want to just quickly talk a bit about the E4 finale.

57:23.480 --> 57:24.280
Yeah, sure.

57:25.080 --> 57:28.600
Okay, so Kenzo Craigie won the championship.

57:29.720 --> 57:31.480
Yay, Kenzo Craigie champion.

57:31.880 --> 57:32.380
Woohoo!

57:33.400 --> 57:38.120
I think R-ace has really made a step up this year compared to last year.

57:38.120 --> 57:43.080
I mean, they've been contending for wins on several circuits instead of, you know,

57:43.080 --> 57:44.840
just Mugello like last year.

57:47.080 --> 57:50.040
And obviously Kenzo's a really talented driver.

57:51.560 --> 57:54.280
And I'm really, really happy that he managed to win the championship,

57:54.280 --> 57:57.080
even if it was vaguely controversial.

57:58.200 --> 58:00.040
For those who didn't watch, basically.

58:01.000 --> 58:03.080
Kenzo was leading the championship.

58:03.080 --> 58:07.240
Race 2 was happening, and he got hit in the back by Noah Killion.

58:08.440 --> 58:10.760
And got taken out of the race.

58:11.720 --> 58:14.760
And so that allowed Sammalisto to close the gap.

58:15.720 --> 58:16.360
By a lot.

58:17.400 --> 58:17.900
Boo!

58:19.160 --> 58:20.520
On to race 3.

58:22.280 --> 58:28.520
By the end of the race, Kenzo was running, I think, P4, I want to say.

58:28.520 --> 58:32.280
And his teammate, Consai was running in P2.

58:32.280 --> 58:34.920
And I think it was Sammalisto in P3.

58:34.920 --> 58:36.760
I don't remember where Sammalisto was, actually.

58:37.640 --> 58:40.520
I think he was making it up, but he wasn't...

58:43.240 --> 58:44.680
I don't remember.

58:45.320 --> 58:49.720
But either way, at the end of the race, you know, final few laps,

58:49.720 --> 58:53.800
Consani slows down, lets Craigie past him.

58:53.800 --> 58:58.120
Which puts Craigie and Sammalisto tied on points.

58:58.200 --> 59:01.240
And Craigie wins the championship on countback.

59:03.160 --> 59:05.880
And, you know, people were like, oh, that's so controversial.

59:05.880 --> 59:07.960
Why would he move for his teammate?

59:07.960 --> 59:09.400
Why is there team orders?

59:09.400 --> 59:15.080
But then the same thing happened with Busso and Sammalisto literally five minutes before?

59:16.280 --> 59:16.780
Yeah.

59:17.320 --> 59:24.760
And Andy wouldn't have needed to move over if, you know, Killion hadn't done his thing.

59:25.720 --> 59:31.560
I think US Racing still ended up winning the championship, like the team's championship.

59:31.560 --> 59:36.680
But R-ace finished first and third in the drivers' championship, which was really, really cool.

59:36.680 --> 59:37.640
I really liked that.

59:38.280 --> 59:38.780
Yeah.

59:39.160 --> 59:39.960
There wasn't really...

59:40.760 --> 59:42.440
Was there other things going on?

59:42.440 --> 59:45.080
Toniolo was surprisingly good this weekend.

59:45.080 --> 59:46.360
I don't know where he came from.

59:47.480 --> 59:48.680
Not sure either.

59:49.960 --> 59:52.760
He was on pole for one of the races, but he got taken out

59:53.480 --> 59:56.520
when Killion crashed into Craigie.

59:58.760 --> 01:00:00.760
Toniolo was kind of collateral damage.

01:00:01.560 --> 01:00:02.600
I feel kind of bad.

01:00:04.280 --> 01:00:09.240
But yeah, outside of the races, do you want to talk about Aksoy?

01:00:10.920 --> 01:00:12.120
So stupid.

01:00:12.120 --> 01:00:12.760
I'm so...

01:00:13.800 --> 01:00:16.120
It's not even something that you can even avoid.

01:00:16.120 --> 01:00:17.880
I don't know how you would avoid that.

01:00:18.280 --> 01:00:24.760
Basically, up until this weekend, Alp Aksoy was running P3 in the standings.

01:00:24.760 --> 01:00:32.040
And then, right before it starts, everyone's looking at the timing screens and he's like

01:00:32.040 --> 01:00:33.000
all the way in the back.

01:00:33.000 --> 01:00:37.240
And then suddenly it's been announced that he's not even at the track.

01:00:37.240 --> 01:00:39.800
He can't even race because he had a visa issue.

01:00:41.400 --> 01:00:42.600
That sucks really bad.

01:00:43.320 --> 01:00:45.000
He couldn't even enter Italy.

01:00:45.800 --> 01:00:49.880
The one thing that I'm upset about, it probably didn't matter as much to him,

01:00:49.880 --> 01:00:53.880
but it was the fact that it was the race weekend of his birthday.

01:00:54.840 --> 01:00:57.960
Like, man, I would have loved to race on my birthday.

01:00:58.680 --> 01:01:02.440
Luckily, the only driver he was overtaken by was Consani.

01:01:02.440 --> 01:01:04.520
But yeah, that sucks.

01:01:06.280 --> 01:01:10.760
So yeah, to summarize the championship standings,

01:01:10.760 --> 01:01:16.520
Craigie P1 on 190 points ahead of Sammalisto on 190 points,

01:01:16.520 --> 01:01:18.280
but like I said, Craigie won on countback.

01:01:18.840 --> 01:01:20.520
Consani won 31 points.

01:01:21.160 --> 01:01:24.440
Luckily for him, moving aside for his teammate,

01:01:24.440 --> 01:01:27.640
didn't actually lose him out on any championship positions,

01:01:28.200 --> 01:01:30.520
which probably made the decision easier.

01:01:31.480 --> 01:01:33.240
I mean, Consani’s had a rough season.

01:01:33.960 --> 01:01:39.640
It's not been great for him, both because of his own luck and also his own mistakes.

01:01:41.000 --> 01:01:42.520
It's been rough.

01:01:42.520 --> 01:01:47.400
So to give up what could have possibly been a win or at least a podium

01:01:47.400 --> 01:01:51.320
for your teammate to win the championship, I really, really liked that.

01:01:51.320 --> 01:01:53.000
I really appreciated it.

01:01:53.880 --> 01:01:58.040
And I thought it was really funny that people on Twitter were like,

01:01:58.760 --> 01:02:00.840
oh yeah, Craigie’s gonna take...

01:02:03.480 --> 01:02:04.280
Craigie’s gonna...

01:02:05.640 --> 01:02:08.040
I'm trying to word this properly.

01:02:08.840 --> 01:02:12.440
Like, Craigie’s gonna invite Consani for dinner.

01:02:13.640 --> 01:02:14.140
Oh.

01:02:14.600 --> 01:02:21.640
Which feels vaguely reminiscent of the big Christmas present for Evan Giltaire.

01:02:22.680 --> 01:02:23.960
It's always some French guy.

01:02:25.080 --> 01:02:26.520
It's always the French guys.

01:02:28.280 --> 01:02:29.960
Do we need to explain what we're referencing?

01:02:29.960 --> 01:02:32.040
I think we need to explain what we're referencing.

01:02:32.040 --> 01:02:37.000
I think especially with the type of, oh, I forgot the word.

01:02:37.800 --> 01:02:42.600
Our reputation as who we both rep, especially on the podcast, it's quite clear.

01:02:42.600 --> 01:02:44.840
To summarize, because I don't want to take too long,

01:02:45.960 --> 01:02:52.520
there was a karting championship in 2022 where KNB and Alex Powell were fighting

01:02:52.520 --> 01:02:53.960
each other for the championship.

01:02:53.960 --> 01:02:58.760
Powell was leading the race and KNB needed to gain a position

01:02:58.760 --> 01:03:00.920
to be able to win the championship over him.

01:03:00.920 --> 01:03:08.360
So, Giltaire, who was ahead of KNB, received team orders to let KNB vie.

01:03:08.360 --> 01:03:10.920
And all three of them were on the podium together.

01:03:11.720 --> 01:03:14.200
And who was the commentator?

01:03:15.480 --> 01:03:16.120
Sanson.

01:03:16.120 --> 01:03:18.440
It was Sanson, because he was the one going...

01:03:19.240 --> 01:03:26.040
Yeah, so Sanson kept saying that KNB will be giving Giltaire a really big Christmas present.

01:03:27.320 --> 01:03:30.600
Yeah, that's the context, because we keep referencing that.

01:03:30.680 --> 01:03:32.120
I feel like people think we're insane.

01:03:37.720 --> 01:03:45.560
Like I said, Consani’s in P3 on 131 points, Aksoy P4 on 112, and Savinkov P5 on 110.

01:03:47.720 --> 01:03:51.320
Moving on to British F4, which also ended that weekend.

01:03:51.880 --> 01:03:55.320
Are we surprised that Dries van Langendonck won the championship?

01:03:56.200 --> 01:03:56.700
No.

01:03:56.700 --> 01:03:57.200
No.

01:03:58.380 --> 01:04:03.500
I think that was the most obvious championship to ever happen.

01:04:04.860 --> 01:04:08.300
Yeah, did he win it in race one?

01:04:08.300 --> 01:04:08.940
I don't remember.

01:04:08.940 --> 01:04:10.300
Was it race one or two?

01:04:10.300 --> 01:04:12.780
I just remember it was on the first day.

01:04:12.780 --> 01:04:15.260
Yeah, I don't remember which race it was, but he won it early.

01:04:15.260 --> 01:04:16.300
That's what I'm trying to say.

01:04:17.020 --> 01:04:18.060
I think it was race one.

01:04:19.260 --> 01:04:23.500
Wasn't it one almost with the qualifying?

01:04:24.060 --> 01:04:27.180
He almost won it in quali, but then he didn't.

01:04:27.180 --> 01:04:31.980
And I think somewhere in an interview he said that he would rather not win it in qualifying

01:04:31.980 --> 01:04:34.300
because that's just a bit anticlimactic or something.

01:04:35.260 --> 01:04:40.460
Yeah, anyways, just for the whole season, I think we saw a lot from him.

01:04:41.100 --> 01:04:42.220
A lot of bad luck.

01:04:42.780 --> 01:04:43.820
Race ban.

01:04:43.820 --> 01:04:45.420
Race ban was funny, actually.

01:04:46.460 --> 01:04:50.300
They tried so hard to not let him win the championship and he won it anyways.

01:04:50.300 --> 01:04:56.060
Do we want to talk a bit about just the general, just a short five-minute recap of the season?

01:04:56.060 --> 01:05:00.060
I want to mourn Ethan Jeff Hall for a second.

01:05:00.060 --> 01:05:07.180
He got dropped by Mercedes and didn't compete in the last two rounds

01:05:07.180 --> 01:05:09.980
and still finished the championship in P5.

01:05:10.780 --> 01:05:12.780
One minute of silence for him, please.

01:05:14.300 --> 01:05:20.140
But he's been testing F4 with LN4 Fusion.

01:05:21.020 --> 01:05:25.180
I don't know if this means he's going to be doing another season of F4 with them

01:05:25.180 --> 01:05:30.220
or if he's just there to help with testing setups and stuff.

01:05:31.180 --> 01:05:41.420
I would like to see him go to FREC with LN4 Fusion because I assume his finances aren't the best.

01:05:42.300 --> 01:05:46.540
I think they need the money from the FREC drivers

01:05:46.540 --> 01:05:47.980
they're rumored to be having

01:05:49.020 --> 01:05:50.860
But I trust rumors.

01:05:50.860 --> 01:05:54.860
I think they've kept F3 under so great wraps,

01:05:54.860 --> 01:06:01.260
I would not be surprised if it's similar for the other series.

01:06:01.260 --> 01:06:08.460
And the rumors come ma inly from the drivers themselves who are like,

01:06:08.460 --> 01:06:09.580
I would love to do it.

01:06:09.580 --> 01:06:12.060
I'm in conversation with them.

01:06:12.060 --> 01:06:15.020
But it's easy to take things out of context

01:06:15.020 --> 01:06:20.140
you know. It's easy to say, oh, that guy said he's in conversation with them,

01:06:20.140 --> 01:06:21.740
that has to mean something.

01:06:21.740 --> 01:06:27.100
When, if I was a driver, I think drivers currently approaching the team

01:06:27.100 --> 01:06:28.940
because it's a great opportunity.

01:06:29.980 --> 01:06:30.860
At least that's my hope.

01:06:32.540 --> 01:06:34.700
I guess we'll find out eventually.

01:06:34.700 --> 01:06:38.300
I don't know if LN4 Fusion are going to be testing.

01:06:39.740 --> 01:06:42.300
Are there still more FREC postseason tests?

01:06:42.300 --> 01:06:43.420
I've kind of forgotten.

01:06:45.260 --> 01:06:48.540
Because they weren't present in the last few postseason tests.

01:06:48.540 --> 01:06:52.140
I don't know if they're going to show up or what's going on over there.

01:06:54.620 --> 01:06:57.820
But yeah, about drivers that aren't DVL,

01:06:59.580 --> 01:07:02.780
the championship ended with Theo Palmer in P2,

01:07:02.780 --> 01:07:04.220
Lewis Wherell in P3.

01:07:05.420 --> 01:07:05.820
Really?

01:07:06.460 --> 01:07:07.260
How did that happen?

01:07:08.620 --> 01:07:11.180
Because Wherell was fighting DVL for the championship.

01:07:11.900 --> 01:07:14.380
Yeah, but Theo Palmer was really consistent.

01:07:14.380 --> 01:07:20.220
Like he was constantly P4 to like P6 in almost every race.

01:07:20.220 --> 01:07:28.140
So he got a lot of points there while Lewis Wherell had some bad runs like Zandvoort

01:07:28.140 --> 01:07:31.740
where he didn't score a single point and some more retirements

01:07:31.740 --> 01:07:33.660
and just non-point finishes.

01:07:34.620 --> 01:07:38.060
Yeah, in P4 is Proudford-Nalder,

01:07:38.060 --> 01:07:40.220
I've actually been pretty impressed by him

01:07:40.220 --> 01:07:45.100
because I think he made his F4 debut in like, halfway through Formula Winter Series.

01:07:47.180 --> 01:07:49.100
So it's not even like he did the entire Winter Series.

01:07:49.100 --> 01:07:51.660
He only did like two rounds, I think?

01:07:51.660 --> 01:07:53.580
So he's had a pretty solid season.

01:07:55.340 --> 01:07:58.700
I think he's been rumored to be stepping up to GB3 next year.

01:07:59.340 --> 01:08:02.140
But yeah, pretty good season from him.

01:08:03.500 --> 01:08:05.420
P5, like I said, is Ethan Jeff Hall.

01:08:06.300 --> 01:08:12.300
A couple other notable drivers, Scott Lindblom ended the season in P7.

01:08:13.340 --> 01:08:16.380
Unfortunately, Peter isn't here to talk about his racecraft.

01:08:17.980 --> 01:08:20.220
Yeah, I know Peter likes to talk about his racecraft

01:08:20.220 --> 01:08:23.660
but I was the slightest bit disappointed.

01:08:23.660 --> 01:08:26.860
I would have liked to see more from him

01:08:26.860 --> 01:08:29.900
and I know he missed one weekend.

01:08:29.900 --> 01:08:32.940
I don't remember why, but I remember- Race ban.

01:08:33.580 --> 01:08:33.820
Yeah.

01:08:33.820 --> 01:08:34.300
Oh, yeah.

01:08:35.420 --> 01:08:39.980
But I remember overall, it was fine.

01:08:39.980 --> 01:08:41.420
It was an alright season.

01:08:42.140 --> 01:08:43.180
He's been a bit messy.

01:08:44.380 --> 01:08:45.740
He could have done more.

01:08:45.740 --> 01:08:48.220
Like it took him way too long.

01:08:48.220 --> 01:08:51.260
He only got one win and it took him way too long to get it.

01:08:51.900 --> 01:08:55.900
And I expected him to be closer to DVL.

01:08:56.540 --> 01:08:59.340
Yeah, and he had a couple of those races where

01:09:00.220 --> 01:09:02.300
as much as Peter likes to praise his racecraft,

01:09:02.300 --> 01:09:06.540
I think he just didn't really have the greatest racecraft in those races.

01:09:08.540 --> 01:09:14.380
There was a race where he ended up crashing someone else out.

01:09:14.380 --> 01:09:18.380
I don't remember what race it was, but I remember the scenes of the race.

01:09:19.100 --> 01:09:22.540
Another one people would probably like to know about,

01:09:22.540 --> 01:09:23.420
Chiara Bättig.

01:09:23.420 --> 01:09:30.540
She's in P13, but she had very clear improvements through the season.

01:09:30.540 --> 01:09:35.340
And if you look at the standings, it's hilarious because you can see post-Zandvoort,

01:09:36.860 --> 01:09:42.460
it's such a way up because up to Zandvoort,

01:09:42.460 --> 01:09:51.260
it's mainly stuck somewhere in like P13 to P17.

01:09:51.900 --> 01:09:55.340
And I remember thinking she struggled a bit in qualifying

01:09:55.340 --> 01:09:59.980
and she was a bit off her teammates where I expected more from her.

01:09:59.980 --> 01:10:05.100
But post-Zandvoort, she locked in and she got a lot of important points.

01:10:05.100 --> 01:10:07.740
She was consistently in the top 10.

01:10:08.940 --> 01:10:10.780
Over the season, she got two podiums.

01:10:11.660 --> 01:10:13.820
It was really good showing from her.

01:10:15.020 --> 01:10:23.340
In the beginning, I was a bit worried, but I was reminded it is her rookie season

01:10:23.980 --> 01:10:29.420
and she did an important improvement and she won some award,

01:10:29.420 --> 01:10:32.380
but I don't remember what it's called, but it's an important award.

01:10:33.340 --> 01:10:36.860
Wasn't it an award for the most improved driver or something along those lines?

01:10:36.860 --> 01:10:41.260
Yeah, the Jake Cook Memorial Award.

01:10:41.260 --> 01:10:42.540
Yeah, thank you.

01:10:43.100 --> 01:10:45.580
It also has something to do with mental health.

01:10:45.580 --> 01:10:49.020
And it's voted by like, I think it was team principals

01:10:49.020 --> 01:10:51.500
and other people working in the paddock.

01:10:51.500 --> 01:10:57.980
And it was pretty much agreed that she had a great improvement across the season.

01:10:57.980 --> 01:11:00.380
And I'm really excited to see what she can do next season.

01:11:01.100 --> 01:11:09.500
And overall, we saw three female podiums, two with Chiara, one with Alba Larsen.

01:11:10.860 --> 01:11:12.060
Great, beautiful.

01:11:12.060 --> 01:11:12.700
I was there.

01:11:13.260 --> 01:11:14.140
I enjoyed it a lot.

01:11:14.860 --> 01:11:17.420
It's been a really interesting British F4 season

01:11:17.420 --> 01:11:22.140
and I think I'm really excited to see what these drivers will do,

01:11:23.340 --> 01:11:29.260
like the top drivers will do in like FREC or Eurocup 3 or GB3 or wherever they decide to go.

01:11:30.220 --> 01:11:33.660
I'm most excited for FREC next year, I think.

01:11:34.620 --> 01:11:36.140
Oh, I can't wait.

01:11:36.140 --> 01:11:41.900
Yeah, I feel like FREC is like, it's kind of like Avengers Endgame, but for racing.

01:11:41.900 --> 01:11:42.700
It's like all these-

01:11:42.700 --> 01:11:45.900
I wanted to say that Eurocup 3 might be interesting

01:11:47.180 --> 01:11:50.940
with, you know, a couple drivers who are rumored to be repeating the season.

01:11:50.940 --> 01:11:54.620
And also I've heard rumors that Consani might be going there,

01:11:54.620 --> 01:11:58.620
but also I've heard rumors that Consani might be doing a third F4 season,

01:11:58.620 --> 01:11:59.980
which is not good.

01:12:00.620 --> 01:12:01.500
RIP Consani.

01:12:03.260 --> 01:12:04.940
Not gone and not forgotten.

01:12:06.380 --> 01:12:08.060
So that's it for today's episode.

01:12:08.060 --> 01:12:09.500
I hope you guys enjoyed.

01:12:09.500 --> 01:12:12.540
On our next episode, we're going to be discussing F1 Academy,

01:12:12.540 --> 01:12:16.140
Eurocup 3, as well as the F3 postseason tests.

01:12:16.140 --> 01:12:19.900
And if anything else comes up, we'll probably be discussing that as well.

01:12:21.980 --> 01:12:26.140
Make sure to follow us on Twitter, Instagram, and TikTok at Grand Prixquel,

01:12:26.140 --> 01:12:27.820
and we'll see you next time.
